  "version": "0.9.0",
  "changes": [
    "Independent v9 package and launchers consolidate the preserved v8 and v8a feature sets.",
    "Retain exposure-normalized source count rates, Ceres/Vesta ephemerides and evidence, saturated-source astrometry, and per-channel masked Moffat-wing diagnostics.",
    "Retain bz2-compressed FITS input, exact supplied-time planet/source association, portable results storage, and append-only SQLite recording.",
    "Keep the exact saved zenith red-X marker and legend entry while omitting its marker-attached on-image text label; numerical products are unchanged.",
    "Use great-circle arcminute gates throughout planet association and recover significant metadata-predicted peaks rejected only by undersampled morphology, without admitting them to stellar astrometry.",
    "Compress page-one interpretation prose while retaining numerical tables and one strongest measured statement per planet; distinguish fixed-time associations from the independent epoch fit.",
    "Report a retained single-planet blind candidate's date, local uncertainty and residual as unconfirmed evidence without promoting it to an adopted epoch."
  ],
